    "crowd": {
      "about": "Fans come from the Blender crowd kit (tools/blender/crowd, assets/actors/crowd/manifest.json). Near the wearer they are real meshes frozen in poses (lod0, lod1); farther out, multi-angle impostor cards. Clothing is tinted per matchup from the kit's mask: R the club chip, G `secondary`, B face paint. Fans move by group: a group swaps pose (a mesh, or an atlas row), never skins per fan on the CPU. The away section is bowl.crowd.awaySection. About a third of each section wears no club colour (`neutrals`), and every fan's club colour takes its own value and saturation, so a stand is a mass, not two flat hues. Far cards are softened toward each fan's mean (`cardContrast`) and split into interleaved `cardVariants` per slice with jittered edges, so a pose change never draws a vertical stripe.",
      "assets": {
        "impostorNormal": "actors/crowd/impostor_normal.png"
      },
      "models": {
        "lod0Poses": "actors/crowd/lod0_poses.usdz",
        "lod1Poses": "actors/crowd/lod1_poses.usdz",
        "lod2Poses": "actors/crowd/lod2_poses.usdz"
      },
